  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `{cite}` of `requirements.cli.mdbook` on `struct[Definition]` (src/lib.rs:121-126) is the right role.\n\n- **Not a test.** `Definition` is a plain data struct holding `path`, `text` and `kind`. It is not a test or test helper.\n- **Not an impl.** The struct makes no decision and performs no check. It also does not constrain anything the requirement states. The requirement says only that `habeas mdbook` acts as the preprocessor, renders definitions and badges, and that `book.toml` configures the `habeas` preprocessor through a Cargo alias. The preprocessing itself is in `fn[preprocess_book]` (src/lib.rs:176-272), which carries `{impl}` for this requirement.\n- **A reasonable cite.** `preprocess_book` builds a `Definition` for each closed definition block in the book's chapters. The badge functions `reference_badge`, `replace_references` and `replace_inline_references` take `BTreeMap<String, Definition>` to link badges to their targets. `render_detail_page` reads `definition.path`, `definition.text` and `definition.kind`. Because the struct's shape serves the mdBook preprocessor's rendering, a change to what the preprocessor must render could require changing it. That fits `{cite}`.\n- **No redundancy.** The struct has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same requirement, so the cite is not redundant.\n\nI found no gap.",
